Here are examples demonstrating different ways to use `@Autowired` and `@Qualifier` in Spring:

### 1. **Field Injection with `@Autowired`**
```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class FieldInjectionExample {
    @Autowired
    private Service service;

    public void doSomething() {
        service.perform();
    }
}

@Component
class Service {
    public void perform() {
        System.out.println("Service performing task");
    }
}
```

### 2. **Setter Injection with `@Autowired`**
```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class SetterInjectionExample {
    private Service service;

    @Autowired
    public void setService(Service service) {
        this.service = service;
    }

    public void doSomething() {
        service.perform();
    }
}

@Component
class Service {
    public void perform() {
        System.out.println("Service performing task");
    }
}
```

### 3. **Constructor Injection with `@Autowired`**
```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class ConstructorInjectionExample {
    private final Service service;

    @Autowired
    public ConstructorInjectionExample(Service service) {
        this.service = service;
    }

    public void doSomething() {
        service.perform();
    }
}

@Component
class Service {
    public void perform() {
        System.out.println("Service performing task");
    }
}
```

### 4. **Using `@Qualifier` with `@Autowired` (Field Injection)**
If you have multiple beans of the same type, use `@Qualifier` to specify which one to inject.

```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Qualifier;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class FieldInjectionWithQualifier {
    @Autowired
    @Qualifier("specificService")
    private Service service;

    public void doSomething() {
        service.perform();
    }
}

@Component("specificService")
class SpecificService implements Service {
    public void perform() {
        System.out.println("Specific Service performing task");
    }
}

@Component("anotherService")
class AnotherService implements Service {
    public void perform() {
        System.out.println("Another Service performing task");
    }
}

interface Service {
    void perform();
}
```

