To throw an error if any field is missing in your `rawStyles` object when comparing it to your `GlobalStyleProps` type, you can use a helper function that checks if all required keys from `GlobalStyleProps` exist in `rawStyles`. If any key is missing, the function will throw an error.

Here's how you can modify your `getStyles` function:

```ts
import rawStyles from "../styles/combined-v5.module.css";

export type GlobalStyleProps = {
  "component-selection-section": string;
  main: string;
  header: string;
  img: string;
  ul: string;
  label: string;
  input: string;
  button: string;
  form: string;
  infobox: string;
  "infobox-hint": string;
  "infobox-warning": string;
  "warning--low": string;
  "warning--medium": string;
  "warning--high": string;
  "add-timer": string;
  "blog-posts": string;
  "loading-fallback": string;
  error: string;
  "nav-button": string;
  select: string;
  "info-box": string;
  "info-box-detail": string;
  post: string;
  "post-author": string;
  "post-body": string;
  posts: string;
};

// Function to assert that the rawStyles object matches the GlobalStyleProps type
const getStyles = (): GlobalStyleProps => {
  const expectedKeys: Array<keyof GlobalStyleProps> = [
    "component-selection-section",
    "main",
    "header",
    "img",
    "ul",
    "label",
    "input",
    "button",
    "form",
    "infobox",
    "infobox-hint",
    "infobox-warning",
    "warning--low",
    "warning--medium",
    "warning--high",
    "add-timer",
    "blog-posts",
    "loading-fallback",
    "error",
    "nav-button",
    "select",
    "info-box",
    "info-box-detail",
    "post",
    "post-author",
    "post-body",
    "posts",
  ];

  // Check if any expected key is missing in rawStyles
  expectedKeys.forEach((key) => {
    if (!(key in rawStyles)) {
      throw new Error(`Missing key "${key}" in rawStyles`);
    }
  });

  // Cast rawStyles to GlobalStyleProps (after ensuring all keys are present)
  return rawStyles as GlobalStyleProps;
};

// Hook to return the global styles and the raw styles
export const useGlobalStyles = () => {
  const GLOBAL_APPLICATION_STYLES = getStyles();
  return {
    GLOBAL_APPLICATION_STYLES,
    rawStyles,
  };
};
```

### How it works:
1. **`expectedKeys`:** This array contains all the keys from your `GlobalStyleProps` type.
2. **Check if each key exists in `rawStyles`:** The `forEach` loop goes through each key in `expectedKeys` and checks if it exists in `rawStyles`. If a key is missing, it throws an error.
3. **Returning `rawStyles`:** If all the required keys are present, it returns `rawStyles` cast to `GlobalStyleProps`.

Now, if any key from `GlobalStyleProps` is missing in `rawStyles`, an error will be thrown.

