Here's the implementation of a Higher-Order Component (HOC) called `withModal` that wraps a component in the `ModalV2` and provides `onClose` functionality:

### `withModal.tsx` (HOC)

```tsx
import React, { ReactNode } from 'react';
import ModalV2 from './ModalV2'; // Adjust the import path if necessary

// The HOC function
const withModal = <P extends object>(
  WrappedComponent: React.ComponentType<P>
) => {
  // The component that will be returned by the HOC
  return (props: P & { onClose: () => void }) => {
    const { onClose } = props;

    return (
      <ModalV2 onClose={onClose}>
        <WrappedComponent {...props} />
      </ModalV2>
    );
  };
};

export default withModal;
```

### Example usage of `withModal`:

