Here's the `useTreeData` custom hook that encapsulates the logic for processing tree data, which you can use in the `ReactArcherApp10` component:

```javascript
import { useMemo } from "react";
import { addLevelAndParentIdField, flattenTreeData, filterByLevel } from "../../common/utils/array-operation-utils";

const useTreeData = (data) => {
    const dataWithLevelAndParentIdField = useMemo(() => addLevelAndParentIdField(data), [data]);

    const flattenedData = useMemo(() => flattenTreeData(dataWithLevelAndParentIdField), [dataWithLevelAndParentIdField]);

    const levelCompArr = useMemo(() => {
        let currentLevel = 0;
        const levelComponentArr = [];

        while (true) {
            const levelArr = filterByLevel(flattenedData, currentLevel);
            if (levelArr.length === 0) break;
            levelComponentArr.push({ level: currentLevel, levelData: levelArr });
            currentLevel++;
        }

        return levelComponentArr;
    }, [flattenedData]);

    return { dataWithLevelAndParentIdField, levelCompArr };
};

export default useTreeData;
```

### How to Use `useTreeData` in `ReactArcherApp10`

Now, update the `ReactArcherApp10` component to use this custom hook:

