The warning message, *No name was provided for external module "react/jsx-runtime" in "output.globals"* occurs because Vite/Rollup is unsure of the global variable name to use for the external module `react/jsx-runtime`. This happens because `react/jsx-runtime` is part of React 17+ for JSX transformations, and you need to explicitly define it in the `globals` option.

Here's how you can fix this issue:

---

### **Update `vite.config.ts`**
Add `jsxRuntime` to the `globals` option under `rollupOptions.output`:

```ts
import { defineConfig } from "vite";
import { resolve } from "path";
import dts from "vite-plugin-dts";
import react from "@vitejs/plugin-react";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react(), dts({ include: ["lib"] })],
  build: {
    lib: {
      entry: resolve(__dirname, "lib/main.ts"),
      name: "ReactJsLibraryWithVite", // UMD global name
      fileName: (format) => `index.${format}.js`,
      formats: ["es", "cjs", "umd"], // Include CommonJS build
    },
    rollupOptions: {
      external: ["react", "react/jsx-runtime", "react-dom"], // Mark peer dependencies as external
      output: {
        globals: {
          react: "React",
          "react-dom": "ReactDOM",
          "react/jsx-runtime": "jsxRuntime", // Add this line
        },
      },
    },
  },
});
```

---

### **Why It Works**
The `rollupOptions.output.globals` map is used to specify the global variable names for external dependencies when building UMD bundles. Since `react/jsx-runtime` is a separate module, it also needs an entry in the `globals` object.

---

### **Optional: Suppress Warnings**
If you don’t want to see these warnings but still want Vite to handle the global name automatically, you can suppress this specific warning by customizing Vite's build logging:

```ts
build: {
  rollupOptions: {
    onwarn(warning, warn) {
      if (warning.code === "UNRESOLVED_IMPORT" && warning.source === "react/jsx-runtime") {
        return;
      }
      warn(warning);
    },
  },
}
```

---

### **After Changes**
Run the build command again:

```bash
npm run build-lib
```

The warning should no longer appear, and your UMD bundle will correctly handle `react/jsx-runtime`.

