Here’s the modified version of the `NestedArrayBuilder` to utilize the `Section` class:

### Modified Code:
```javascript
class Section {
  constructor(title, subSections = [], questions = []) {
    this.title = title;
    this.subSections = subSections;
    this.questions = questions;
  }
}

export class NestedArrayBuilder {
  constructor() {
    this.structure = [];
    this.currentSection = null;
    this.currentSubSection = null;
  }

  addSection(title) {
    const section = new Section(title);
    this.structure.push(section);
    this.currentSection = section;
    this.currentSubSection = null; // Reset currentSubSection
    return this; // Enable chaining
  }

  addSubSection(subSectionTitle) {
    if (!this.currentSection) {
      throw new Error("You must add a section before adding a sub-section.");
    }
    const subSection = new Section(subSectionTitle);
    this.currentSection.subSections.push(subSection);
    this.currentSubSection = subSection;
    return this; // Enable chaining
  }

  addQuestion(question) {
    if (!this.currentSubSection) {
      throw new Error("You must add a sub-section before adding a question.");
    }
    this.currentSubSection.questions.push(question);
    return this; // Enable chaining
  }

  addQuestions(...questions) {
    if (!this.currentSubSection) {
      throw new Error("You must add a sub-section before adding questions.");
    }
    this.currentSubSection.questions.push(...questions);
    return this; // Enable chaining
  }

  build() {
    return this.structure;
  }
}
```

### Key Changes:
1. **`Section` Class Integration**:
   - Each section and sub-section is now an instance of the `Section` class.
   - `subSections` and `questions` are initialized as arrays in the `Section` constructor.

2. **Updated Methods**:
   - `addSection`: Creates a new `Section` instance and appends it to the `structure`.
   - `addSubSection`: Adds a `Section` instance as a sub-section to the `currentSection`.
   - `addQuestion` and `addQuestions`: Add questions to the `currentSubSection`'s `questions` array.

3. **State Management**:
   - Reset `currentSubSection` whenever a new section is added, ensuring proper hierarchy.

### Example Usage:
```javascript
