Yes, you can use a **custom annotation** along with **reflection** to automatically validate the `values` object against the fields of the `Student` entity. This approach avoids hardcoding valid keys and makes the process more dynamic and maintainable.

---

### Step-by-Step Implementation

#### 1. **Custom Annotation**
Define an annotation to specify the class whose fields should be used for validation.

```java
import java.lang.annotation.ElementType;
import java.lang.annotation.Retention;
import java.lang.annotation.RetentionPolicy;
import java.lang.annotation.Target;

@Target(ElementType.TYPE)
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
public @interface ValidateKeys {
    Class<?> value(); // The class to validate against
}
```

---

#### 2. **PatchRequest Class**
Add the `@ValidateKeys` annotation to the `PatchRequest` class, specifying the `Student` entity as the validation target.

```java
import jakarta.validation.constraints.NotNull;
import java.util.Map;

@ValidateKeys(Student.class) // Specify the validation target
public class PatchRequest {
    @NotNull
    private String uniqueId;

    @NotNull
    private Map<String, Object> values;

    // Getters and Setters
    public String getUniqueId() {
        return uniqueId;
    }

    public void setUniqueId(String uniqueId) {
        this.uniqueId = uniqueId;
    }

    public Map<String, Object> getValues() {
        return values;
    }

    public void setValues(Map<String, Object> values) {
        this.values = values;
    }
}
```

---

#### 3. **Custom Validator**
Create a utility class to validate keys dynamically based on the fields of the specified class.

```java
import java.lang.reflect.Field;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.Set;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class RequestValidator {

    public static void validatePatchRequest(Object request) {
        ValidateKeys validateKeys = request.getClass().getAnnotation(ValidateKeys.class);
        if (validateKeys == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Missing @ValidateKeys annotation on request class.");
        }

        // Get all field names of the target class
        Set<String> validKeys = Set.of(validateKeys.value().getDeclaredFields())
                .stream()
                .map(Field::getName)
                .collect(Collectors.toSet());

        // Extract "values" field from the request object
        try {
            Field valuesField = request.getClass().getDeclaredField("values");
            valuesField.setAccessible(true);
            Map<String, Object> values = (Map<String, Object>) valuesField.get(request);

            // Check if all keys in "values" are valid
            for (String key : values.keySet()) {
                if (!validKeys.contains(key)) {
                    throw new InvalidKeysException("Invalid key: " + key);
                }
            }
        } catch (NoSuchFieldException | IllegalAccessException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Error during validation", e);
        }
    }
}
```

