### Updating the Parent Entity (`Problem`):
Ensure that when you update the `descriptions` field in a `Problem` entity, you only replace or modify the specific description matching the `id`. Here's an example of how to handle updates:

```java
public Optional<Problem> updateDescription(String problemId, ProblemDescription updatedDescription) {
    Optional<Problem> problem = problemRepository.findById(problemId);
    problem.ifPresent(p -> {
        p.getDescriptions().stream()
          .filter(desc -> desc.getId().equals(updatedDescription.getId()))
          .findFirst()
          .ifPresent(desc -> {
              desc.setDetail(updatedDescription.getDetail());
              desc.setLanguage(updatedDescription.getLanguage());
          });
        problemRepository.save(p);
    });
    return problem;
}
