To create a flexible solution that allows you to add any children and only abstracts necessary logic (such as error handling, form submission, etc.), we can enhance the previous HOC so that it doesn't impose any specific form structure. Instead, it should only handle the shared logic like managing state, error handling, submission, and modal control, while leaving the rest (form structure, validation, etc.) to be defined by the wrapped component.

